From f1a6095f9ea075c43e9b170ad4335517700744ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 04:55:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] v2: remove the ZeroMQ notification interface

Lotus V2 does not publish blocks and transactions over ZeroMQ; clients
use Chronik's WebSocket for push notifications. Remove the interface
and everything that only existed for it.

- Delete src/zmq/ (publishers, notification interface, the
  getzmqnotifications RPC) and cmake/modules/FindZeroMQ.cmake.
- init.cpp: drop the -zmqpub* and -zmqpub*hwm options (including the
  hidden-argument fallback), notifier creation, registration and
  shutdown, the RPC registration and the socket-address checks.
- Remove OptionsCategory::ZMQ and its help group, and the "zmq" log
  category. Bit 5 of BCLog::LogFlags stays unused rather than
  renumbering the other categories.
- CMake: remove the BUILD_ZMQ option, its deprecation alias, the native
  build flag and the ENABLE_ZMQ config define. A stale -DBUILD_ZMQ=ON
  now fails configuration with an explicit message; -DBUILD_ZMQ=OFF is
  still accepted and ignored.
- Tests: drop is_zmq_compiled, the ENABLE_ZMQ config.ini entry, the Zmq
  help category in rpc_help.py, the check-doc.py exceptions and the
  TSan suppressions. feature_config_args.py checks that -zmqpubhashblock
  is now rejected as an unknown parameter.

-zmq* options are not accepted for compatibility: V2 is a new chain and
a misconfigured client should fail at startup rather than wait for
notifications that never come. The logging RPC now reports 27
categories.

Tier: V2

Coordinator integration provenance (network403):
Native Qt/ZeroMQ dependency removal preserves new HTTP2/nghttp2 feature flags, helper configuration and OpenSSL3.5 chain; no removed Qt/ZMQ code is restored.
Original scripted commands/hashes above are original-author provenance; modified parent/tool/catalog hashes are not claimed to reproduce this composition. Exact coordinator adaptation scripts and ordered tree proof are in composed403-network-metrics-delivery. Build/runtime/benchmarks NOT_RUN for this composition under user compile-first policy.

Coordinator integration provenance (reference405):
Preserve earlier purposeful source repairs through downstream consumer/context adaptations; exact conflict ledger retained.
All60 authored input payloads retained, with prerequisite-aware same-purpose splits; distinct legacy-index and inherited CXX compatibility remain independent. Pre-format source equals exact403+all60 control tree95718fceff83364b74294a751bd752b2f1a4e384. Only pinnedRuff import/format cleanup follows. Original author commands/hashes are historical reference evidence, not combined405 approval. Reference OFF/native/Rust full gates are preserved separately; combined compile/runtime NOT_RUN.
